   "id": "kospi-black-friday",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Korean stocks tumble 6% as the AI worry spreads from Wall Street",
   "when": "Fri 6 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "KOSPI closed down 6.02% at 5,059.69 after dipping below 5,000 and triggering a circuit breaker. SK hynix lost 10.44% and Samsung Electronics 6.35%; together they are about 40% of the index. Triggers were US plans to tighten AI data centre rules after the midterms and doubts that the AI boom can last. Officials discussed emergency steps, including a three-month relief on collateral rules for investor loans.",
   "why": "SCBKEQTG (15.1%) and EWY (1.9%) are Korea funds heavy in these two chipmakers. SCBKEQTG's NAV on the dashboard is dated 4 Nov, so the Friday fall is not in your numbers yet. KOSPI is down about 11% since that date.",
